{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">2000 AMC 12 #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">2000 AMC 10 #23</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mean\" title=\"Mean\">mean</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median\" title=\"Median\">median</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mode\" title=\"Mode\">mode</a> of the list\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15a3e937aa574fc69dcbb923898a66dfcfe44ee3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10,2,5,2,4,2,x\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>are arranged in increasing order, they form a non-constant <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_progression\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Arithmetic progression\">arithmetic progression</a>. What is the sum of all possible real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b21becaa0a1748ea2532406a48d6d52f07015775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text {(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text {(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\text {(D)}\\ 17 \\qquad \\text {(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>The mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/91493c21139bcb47bae7d578e0f44e87f0cafe19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10+2+5+2+4+2+x}{7} = \\frac{25+x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"288\" height=\"37\" />.</li>\n<li>Arranged in increasing order, the list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2ac6cab5ec93adeed033332d123651dd9f04b1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,2,2,4,5,10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />, so the median is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502b2c2316cfc08a9a57d1232b6d1048e38dfbcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> depending upon the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.</li>\n<li>The mode is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since it appears three times.</li></ul>\n<p>We apply casework upon the median:\n</p>\n<ul><li>If the median is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a83b5560e80995a1ad8c86a0e8880a31ad256b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />), then the arithmetic progression must be constant.</li>\n<li>If the median is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52006e1f8b5b26a6eb40c6fd4086db1965ed691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />), because the mode is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the mean can either be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be4c8ad616823e66107b042e6972394f2fdfffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,3,6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> to form an arithmetic progression. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7ccb3359955321c5ee9a1b46067e31b97bd4dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-25,-4,17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, of which only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> works because it is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>If the median is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/2/8c23ab99cc25ac30f2f5b3ff1caf84d539e7b37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le x \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />), we must have the arithmetic progression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1ee626cc825ebc10ff0ea3a4c9d60d90ac4b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, x, \\frac{25+x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />.  Thus, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e17c092584d868f0b3bd26203ffc85416b40aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x=2+\\frac{25+x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/0342a75a3749e244b0c2968684c67db80673a6f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 17 = \\boxed{20\\ \\mathrm{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"137\" height=\"32\" />.\n-Error fixed(BIGFOOT09) Changes Copyrighted©\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The mode will always be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as there are already <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them.  \nThe median will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> new number is added.  \nThe mean will be all the numbers added together divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>However:\nThe median can't actually be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as that makes it no longer an arithmetic progression.  \nTherefore, the median has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When the median is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as well, as it becomes the median.  \nTherefore, the mean has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which also happens to work when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When the median is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as well as allowing the mean to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  \nAs the current values added together equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we need a number that will allow us to make the mean equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de3a49a6b02c0b0d890fe19b6ad69303a4179636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 7 = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />.  \nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/eccbf23270d38f41e520bfa16597ee48addab057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42-25=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0e7fd6c927bf9f2a68dcfa985dcda2c8574ffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The question asks for the sum of all solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/0342a75a3749e244b0c2968684c67db80673a6f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 17 = \\boxed{20\\ \\mathrm{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"137\" height=\"32\" />.\n~Particle Physics\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/G4c2oCtupTg?si=9qvUkai-YU9sDwY-&amp;t=627\">https://youtu.be/G4c2oCtupTg?si=9qvUkai-YU9sDwY-&amp;t=627</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IziHKOubUI8?t=933\">https://youtu.be/IziHKOubUI8?t=933</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">